  "body": "What happens: the release gate of the v0.20.0 cut is red in the kernel suites. The test `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (`crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`) fails on `testdata/models/bspline_discontinuous.step`.\n\nEvidence (local release gate, Windows, head `182b7018a`, log `gate-logs/release-20261114-185541/02-kernel_suites.log`):\n\n```\nthread 'step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name' panicked at crates\\kernel\\tests\\step_util\\mod.rs:56:19:\nbspline_discontinuous.step: no answer 30s after its cancel (timed out waiting on channel) - a hang or a panic\ntest result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; ... finished in 90.46s\n```\n\nThe reader did not answer in the time limit and did not answer 30 s after the cancel. The files before it in the list (`Block-w-slot.step`, `Milling-test-inch.step`, `Milling-test.step`, `bad_entity_mid_data.step`, `box.step`) gave an answer.\n\nExpected: a degenerate STEP file gives a named refusal in the time limit, or the reader obeys the cancel. A hang on an input file is against the Prime Directive.\n\nNot known: which reader hangs (solidcore, truck or the tessellation), and if the cause is the file or the load of the gate on the machine. The batch gate on main `4f4edcf35` did not run this suite (kernel runs in the release tier only).\n\nDone means:\n- The cause is named.\n- `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` passes in the release tier.\n- A reader that hangs on this file refuses it by name or obeys the cancel, with a test that pins it.\n",
